# {{packageName}}

Jinn external harness impl for `{{solverTypeString}}` on `{{network}}`.

## Quickstart

```bash
yarn install
yarn test       # unit tests
yarn build      # produces dist/
```

Edit `src/index.ts` to plug in your forecasting pipeline. The `run()` method receives a `HarnessContext` (intent + workingDir + capability handles) and returns a `Solution`.

## Publishing

1. Compute your tarball CID + sha256: `npm pack && ipfs add *.tgz` and `shasum -a 256 *.tgz`.
2. Update `jinn.manifest.json` with the resulting CID + hash.
3. Sign the manifest with your ed25519 key (see `spec/2026-05-executor-trust-boundary.md` §5.2).
4. Pin tarball + signed manifest on IPFS.
5. Operators install via `jinn harnesses add ipfs://<manifest-cid>`.

